# Scenario bench-lamp-idle (plan 08-18, D-23, D-39): a benchmark workload, not a test of behaviour. The program is "Lamp Tone"
# (fixtures/FX-demo-lamp-tone-1), entered through the project boot stub contract 2 with the zero graphics ROM and no EXEC image,
# with no input line, run for 120 frames (7,168,320 ticks, about two seconds of guest time). It has no assert and no capture: its
# only oracle is the self-recorded repeatability golden data/golden/bench-lamp-idle.digests (written by ivs-run --update-golden, tier
# deterministic-repeatability), which tools/bench/bench.c compares with its own report before it reads a clock. The ordinary
# steps of the gate run it in both presets like every scenario of data/expected/runner-scenarios.ids. A throughput figure printed
# for it is never a claim.
ivss 1
id bench-lamp-idle
profile intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
content exec boot-stub-2
content grom zero-grom
content cart lamp-tone.ivsc
run-to 120 frames
